{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "The MAP for the dedicated ages-4-7 kid lane: the ~70-anchor canon Bible PAL Kids is built toward. Built BEFORE the corpus so coverage is measured against the plan, not discovered after sprawl (the adult-corpus lesson).",
    "doctrine": {
      "targets": {
        "launchAnchors": 50,
        "matureAnchors": "70-80",
        "ceilingAnchors": 100,
        "hardStopStories": 150
      },
      "storyDesign": {
        "primaryVariantAxis": "length",
        "coreAnchors": "Short + Full",
        "secondaryAnchors": "Short only at first; earn Full later",
        "comfortRitualAnchors": "Short only",
        "longIsEarned": "Long only for exceptional anchors; not a default",
        "emotionalFraming": "Lives in PAL intro / story framing / recommendation / reflection — NOT separate corpus assets",
        "ambientSound": "Player layer (ambient_sound_type), NOT a corpus variant"
      },
      "anchorPhilosophy": [
        "Famous stories first",
        "No obscure anchor until famous anchors feel exhausted (inverse of the adult named-gap rule)",
        "Depth beats breadth; replayability beats novelty"
      ],
      "secondInterpretationRule": "A second telling of the same passage is allowed ONLY when it covers a different verse range and could carry a different title a kid would not call 'the same one'. Represented as SIBLING anchors (e.g. noah_flood + noah_promise), never as a mood variant.",
      "comfortRitualRule": "type=comfort-ritual entries quote Scripture directly (Psalm 23, Lord's Prayer, Beatitudes). These follow public-domain translation compliance (WEB verbatim), NOT loose retelling rules.",
      "ageCenter": "4-7 (bedtime, parent+child, wonder, repetition). Longer buckets stretch toward 8-9."
    },
    "ageCenter": "4-7",
    "coverageDefinition": {
      "covered": "anchor has >=1 fulfilling story at status APPROVED, AUDIO_PENDING, or DONE",
      "in_progress": "fulfilling stories exist but only at DRAFTED/REVIEW/NEEDS_REWRITE",
      "open": "no fulfilling story yet"
    },
    "fulfillmentMatch": "An anchor is fulfilled by kids_manifest.json stories whose scriptureAnchorId is in this anchor's manifestAnchorIds.",
    "generationStatus": "PAUSED until adult corpus closes (see memory project_kid_stories_deferred).",
    "lastUpdated": "2026-06-14",
    "laneTranslation": "WEB-ONLY (Adam 2026-06-14). DIVINE NAME (Adam 2026-06-15): use 'God' by default, 'the Lord' in a directly-quoted line that needs it ('The Lord is my shepherd'). 'Yahweh' is RARE + DELIBERATE — STORY RULE NOT A QUOTA: use it only when hearing God's name is part of the story (covenant-name stories), don't force ~5% or space them out; ~1-in-20 is the natural result, not a target. Covenant-name anchors: Burning Bush (Exodus 3, 'I AM' = single best), Psalm 23 (1803, done), Elijah at Mount Carmel ('Yahweh is God!'), Moses at Sinai / Ten Commandments. Do NOT use in Creation/Noah/David/Jesus-children/walking-on-water/Jairus/Good-Samaritan/Lost-Sheep etc. INTRODUCE GENTLY the first time with context ('God's special name in the Bible is Yahweh...'), never casually ('Yahweh made the stars' = wrong). Default 'God'; 'the Lord' in quoted lines. Full rule: docs/KID_STORY_PROMPT.md section 2. Still WEB-based (rendering choice, not copyright). No KJV lane. 1803 Psalm 23 = one deliberate instance, NOT to be changed (Adam).",
    "laneVoice": "Kid stories ROTATE narrator voices by content-fit (Adam 2026-06-14: 'different voices for different stories'). For each NEW anchor (1803+) pick the approved voice whose warm register best fits that story's tone; keep a gentle bedtime quality and a mix of male + female narrators (lean male ~60-65% per memory feedback_voice_distribution, use female warmth freely). NOT a single lane voice. Existing 1801 David + 1802 Jonah both use VOICE_DAVID_SHEPHERD and stay as-is (NOT re-rendered, per Adam). Banned voices always excluded (see memory feedback_voice_rules).",
    "productionIdBand": "anchorId is the canonical identity. Each anchor that has authored stories ALSO carries a numeric productionId in the reserved 1801+ band (one number per anchor; lengths are files inside kids/<productionId>/, mirroring the adult traditional/<id>/ layout). The number is a production/distribution handle for the existing numeric-keyed audio chain (compression, R2, T9, manifest audioFilePath); it does NOT replace anchorId. Assign lazily (next free number) when an anchor's first story is written. david_goliath = 1801.",
    "launchCutline": "Each anchor carries launch:true/false. launch:true = the v1 cutline (50 anchors); launch:false = deferred to the mature tier (24 anchors). Launch set = all core-tier anchors + the most-replayable secondary ones; obscure/heavier anchors (Paul's road, Gethsemane, lost coin, wisdom-list comfort entries) deferred. Center stays 4-7."
  },
